# EF Core 10 Breaking Changes for Your Code

## 1. `SetPropertyCalls<T>` → `SetPropertyBuilder<T>`

The type was renamed in EF Core 10. Your manual expression tree construction breaks because it references the old type.

**Fix:**

```csharp
Expression<Func<SetPropertyBuilder<Blog>, SetPropertyBuilder<Blog>>> setters =
    s => s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
if (nameChanged)
{
    var blogParameter = Expression.Parameter(typeof(Blog), "b");
    setters = Expression.Lambda<Func<SetPropertyBuilder<Blog>, SetPropertyBuilder<Blog>>>(
        Expression.Call(
            instance: setters.Body,
            methodName: nameof(SetPropertyBuilder<Blog>.SetProperty),
            typeArguments: new[] { typeof(string) },
            arguments: new Expression[]
            {
                Expression.Lambda<Func<Blog, string>>(
                    Expression.Property(blogParameter, nameof(Blog.Name)), blogParameter),
                Expression.Constant("foo")
            }),
        setters.Parameters);
}
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(setters);
```

Replace all references to `SetPropertyCalls<T>` with `SetPropertyBuilder<T>`.

---

## 2. Complex Types — Duplicate Property Names Now Throw

EF Core 10 no longer auto-generates unique column names when multiple complex properties share the same property name (e.g., `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street`). You must explicitly configure column names.

**Fix:**

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, a => {
        a.Property(x => x.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street");
    });
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, a => {
        a.Property(x => x.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street");
    });
});

// For nested: configure each level explicitly
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, p => {
        p.ComplexProperty(pay => pay.BillingAddress, a => {
            a.Property(x => x.City).HasColumnName("Payment_BillingAddress_City");
        });
    });
});
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — New `CommandSource` Parameter

The `CommandReaderExecuting` (and related) methods now require a `CommandSource` parameter.

**Fix:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        CommandSource commandSource)   // ← new parameter
    { /* logging */ }
}
```

---

**Summary of changes:**
| Issue | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| `SetPropertyCalls<T>` removed | Rename to `SetPropertyBuilder<T>` |
| Duplicate complex-type property names | Explicitly set `HasColumnName()` |
| Diagnostics interface | Add `CommandSource commandSource` parameter |

Check the [EF Core 10 breaking changes docs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/ef/core/what-is-new/ef-core-10.0/breaking-changes) for the complete list.
